// Project tasks configuration. See https://zed.dev/docs/tasks for documentation.
//
// Sends the current editor selection into the running `zediator run` session.
//
// The selection is read from the ZED_* ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (via
// `--from-zed-env`), not passed as arguments. Zed runs tasks through
// `zsh -i -c "<command> <args>"` and interpolates $ZED_SELECTED_TEXT into
// that command line, so passing the selection as an arg makes the shell
// re-execute it (e.g. selecting prose that contains backticks or `mise
// exec` runs those as commands). Reading from the environment avoids this.
//
// `command` uses the built binary by absolute path: a Zed task inherits a
// minimal PATH, so `cargo`/an uninstalled `zediator` are not found, and
// `cargo run` also needs the crate root as cwd. During development,
// `cargo build` keeps this debug binary current. Portable alternative:
// `cargo install --path .` and set "command": "zediator".
[
  {
    "label": "zediator: send selection",
    "command": "$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/target/debug/zediator",
    "args": ["send", "--from-zed-env"],

    "reveal": "never",
  },
]
